<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suspĭcax</span></b> , ācis,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>apt to suspect</i>, <i>distrustful</i>, <i>suspicious.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populus suspicax ob eamque rem mobilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Timoth. 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frater,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					40, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus alicujus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>that excites
				mistrust</i>, <i>suspicious</i>: 
			silentium, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 3, 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ira, 2, 29, 2</span></i> (dub.; bracketed
			by Haase).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
